# The argument of `L2:` is taken as it is written (the book #two-kinds-of-receivers): one written Structure after the colon is the ONE field of the record.
# The Structure is code written in the body, and a record written directly in the executable body runs in place (the author 2026-11-16,
# LMX_blog/2026-11-16.md#unnamed-structure-executes; the book, the paragraph «В исполняемом теле непосредственно записанное выражение…»): its two records run,
# so `seen` is 5 and `after` is 6 after the run, and the dump shows ONE Structure under L2.
# State of the tool: the clean graph still leaves an unnamed Structure in code inert (0 and 0), so this row is RED until the open point «an unnamed
# Structure in code executes in place» is implemented; the pin is the norm's, not the tool's.
# наблюдение явной записью: локалы не публикуются (#flush-receiver-contract)
(
    Observed:
        int: seen 0
        int: after 0
)
@: shared data[0]
L2: (shared\Observed\seen := 5; shared\Observed\after := 6)
